      When Ashleigh Barty retired as the reigning holder, she never played another eligible official singles match. Under the retirement-succession rule, the title therefore passed the day after her retirement announcement to <b>Shelby Rogers</b>, the most recent player to have beaten Barty in eligible official singles. This counts as a lineage transfer, but not as a played title match.
